  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "Given the hyperboloid of two sheets $(x+2)^{2}+{y}^{2}-(z-3)^{2}=-1,$ find its $y$-intercepts.",
  "worked_solution": "To find the $y$-intercepts, we plug $x=0$ and $z=0$ into the equation: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(0+2)^{2}+{y}^{2}-(0-3)^{2} & =-1 \\\\ 4+{y}^{2}-9 & =-1 \\\\ {y}^{2} & =4 \\\\ y & =\\pm 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we get the solutions $y=-2$ and $y=2.$\n\nTherefore, the intercepts with the $y$-axis are $(0,-2,0)$ and $(0,2,0).$",
